WEBVTT

00:01.283 --> 00:04.763
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.799 --> 00:08.067
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:08.102 --> 00:11.637
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.672 --> 00:14.640
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.675 --> 00:18.143
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.179 --> 00:21.447
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.482 --> 00:23.015
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.050 --> 00:24.783
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.819 --> 00:29.955
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.864 --> 00:37.996
What the hell?

00:38.032 --> 00:41.033
Oh, hey, Brian.
I was sick of waiting my turn

00:41.068 --> 00:42.534
outside the supermarket,

00:42.570 --> 00:45.137
so I bought every coin-operated
horse in town.

00:45.172 --> 00:46.739
I assume you're on the unicorn?

00:46.774 --> 00:48.440
You know me well, sir.

00:48.476 --> 00:49.842
Must be a dozen horses here.

00:49.877 --> 00:51.276
How do you possibly have the money

00:51.312 --> 00:52.511
for this type of stuff?

00:52.546 --> 00:54.747
Well, I'll tell you,
but only on one condition.

00:54.782 --> 00:56.982
- Fine. Never mind then.
- Investing!

00:57.017 --> 00:58.383
I invest in the stock market.

00:58.419 --> 00:59.918
The stock market? Ugh.

00:59.954 --> 01:01.920
What do you even know about that stuff?

01:01.956 --> 01:04.823
It's easy... I just follow trends
and invest accordingly.

01:04.859 --> 01:07.025
For instance,
there are more single people

01:07.061 --> 01:08.460
over 50 than ever.

01:08.496 --> 01:11.296
So I'm investing in handguns
and blackout window shades.

01:11.332 --> 01:13.398
They don't want to be part
of society, Brian.

01:13.434 --> 01:15.000
They've made that very clear.

01:15.035 --> 01:16.135
I don't know, Stewie, if you ask me,

01:16.170 --> 01:17.870
the stock market's just a rigged game

01:17.905 --> 01:20.205
where the top one-percent
make out like bandits,

01:20.241 --> 01:21.640
and regular people get hurt.

01:21.675 --> 01:23.542
Are you reading off
a teleprompter right now?

01:23.577 --> 01:26.011
No.

01:26.046 --> 01:27.579
The prompter's down. What do we do?

01:27.615 --> 01:28.947
Brian, vamp!

01:28.983 --> 01:32.151
So, great to be in Quahog,
Rhode Island today.

01:32.186 --> 01:34.419
That's why he's the best.

01:38.626 --> 01:41.293
Our top story,
an austere monetary policy

01:41.328 --> 01:43.629
has the European Union
on the brink of collapse,

01:43.664 --> 01:45.564
threatening the entire global economy.

01:45.599 --> 01:48.667
And for viewers making
less than $40,000 a year,

01:48.702 --> 01:52.137
your top story is a big
UFC fight this Saturday.

01:52.173 --> 01:53.939
Wow, I can't wait to see that fight!

01:53.974 --> 01:55.841
Me and the guys are gonna
watch it at the Clam.

01:55.876 --> 01:58.110
Peter, we have dinner
with my parents that night.

01:58.145 --> 02:00.846
It's my mom's birthday.
You have to be there.

02:00.881 --> 02:02.681
Lois, if you let me out of this,

02:02.716 --> 02:05.083
I will go to Meg's
ballet recital in your place.

02:05.119 --> 02:06.385
Deal.

02:11.892 --> 02:14.459
<i>I did not go to the recital.</i>

02:17.531 --> 02:19.731
Whew, what a day.

02:19.767 --> 02:22.401
I asked Ms. Watson if she has
any kids of her own.

02:22.436 --> 02:25.270
Immediately she put me in a time-out.

02:25.306 --> 02:27.206
What the hell?!

02:27.241 --> 02:29.074
<i>Ay, d├нos mio!</i>

02:29.109 --> 02:30.642
Oh, great. Course it's one of them.

02:30.678 --> 02:32.477
- What?!
- Stewie, adults are allowed

02:32.513 --> 02:34.813
to say racist things because of traffic.

02:34.849 --> 02:37.716
Oh, my poor '98 Toyota Corolla.

02:37.751 --> 02:40.619
We all have '98 Toyota Corolla.

02:40.654 --> 02:43.222
<i>- Qu├й?
- I allowed to say racist things</i>

02:43.257 --> 02:45.290
because of traffic.

02:45.326 --> 02:47.159
Well, don't get so angry.
Just tell your insurance

02:47.194 --> 02:48.527
what happened and then they'll...

02:48.562 --> 02:50.596
Oh, you're driving away because
you don't have insurance.

02:50.631 --> 02:54.233
This sucks. Fixing the bumper
is gonna cost at least a grand.

02:54.268 --> 02:55.634
Tell you what, give me a hundred bucks

02:55.669 --> 02:57.870
to put in the stock market,
and I'll take care of it.

02:57.905 --> 02:58.905
The market?

02:58.939 --> 03:00.339
Brian, you won't lose your money.

03:00.374 --> 03:01.440
I promise.

03:01.475 --> 03:03.141
All right, fine.

03:03.177 --> 03:05.944
Guess I'm not the first person
to cave into family pressure.

03:05.980 --> 03:07.746
Like Stephen Baldwin.

03:07.781 --> 03:10.082
Why aren't you a bloated alcoholic yet?

03:10.117 --> 03:12.484
I'm sorry, Ma!

03:19.260 --> 03:20.893
What the hell?

03:20.928 --> 03:23.896
Jerome, what are you doing?
The fight's tonight!

03:23.931 --> 03:26.098
Sorry, fellas, I just got a call.

03:26.133 --> 03:27.566
My mom had a stroke.

03:27.601 --> 03:29.635
I've got to go back
to Long Island to see her.

03:29.670 --> 03:31.036
Hey, a Mets fan, huh?

03:31.071 --> 03:32.671
No, no, Joe, now is not the time

03:32.706 --> 03:34.640
to use your new conversation techniques.

03:34.675 --> 03:37.376
I love her so much. Look at her.

03:37.411 --> 03:39.845
So beautiful.

03:39.880 --> 03:41.513
And there's no one to take care of her,

03:41.548 --> 03:44.049
so, unfortunately,
I'll be gone for a while.

03:44.084 --> 03:46.151
I got to close this place for a month.

03:46.186 --> 03:48.287
- A month?!
- I wish it was February.

03:48.322 --> 03:50.789
'Cause, you know,
that's the shortest month.

03:50.824 --> 03:52.791
Nice one, Joe. You're on the board.

03:52.826 --> 03:54.960
Look, I don't want to
close the place either.

03:54.995 --> 03:56.662
But I don't have anyone to run it.

03:56.697 --> 03:59.097
Really? Well, uh, you know,

03:59.133 --> 04:00.732
we know this place better than anyone.

04:00.768 --> 04:02.367
- What if we run it for you?
- Yeah!

04:02.403 --> 04:04.469
- That's a great idea!
- B-story!

04:04.505 --> 04:07.606
Wow, you fellas would really
watch this place for me?

04:07.641 --> 04:09.908
Are you kidding?
Running a bar is my dream!

04:09.944 --> 04:12.244
Well, that and waking up a rooster.

04:17.718 --> 04:19.484
Dah!

04:19.520 --> 04:21.386
Enjoy the rest of your Saturday.

04:26.260 --> 04:27.693
Hey, Brian, I need to talk to you

04:27.728 --> 04:29.461
about that money I invested for you.

04:29.496 --> 04:31.430
I knew it. You lost it all, didn't you?

04:31.465 --> 04:32.864
God, I never should have
given you my money.

04:32.900 --> 04:35.801
The stock market is a sucker's
bet, like chasing your tail.

04:35.836 --> 04:38.503
God, it's right there,
and yet a million miles away.

04:38.539 --> 04:40.005
What are the physics of that?!

04:40.040 --> 04:42.774
I didn't lose your money, Brian.
Quite the contrary.

04:42.810 --> 04:44.810
Here's a thousand to fix your car.

04:44.845 --> 04:46.345
And here's a thousand profit.

04:46.380 --> 04:47.846
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hold on.

04:47.881 --> 04:50.349
You made $2,000 in a couple days?

04:50.384 --> 04:52.050
- Yep.
- Oh, my God.

04:52.086 --> 04:53.952
You got to teach me how to invest.

04:53.988 --> 04:56.521
Okay, but I can see this is
going to be a lot of work.

04:56.557 --> 05:00.125
So in return, you must teach me Gymkata:

05:00.160 --> 05:02.961
the fusion of gymnastics and karate.

05:02.997 --> 05:06.431
No, Stewie, I won't do that.
It's too dangerous.

05:06.467 --> 05:08.934
I swore I'd never teach Gymkata again.

05:08.969 --> 05:11.470
Brian, there's a 22-year-old
Mongolian heiress

05:11.505 --> 05:13.305
who's being held captive
in a mountain fortress

05:13.340 --> 05:15.173
that happens to have
a pommel horse in it.

05:15.209 --> 05:16.842
There's no other way.

05:42.903 --> 05:45.370
Okay, I'm back. Ready to invest?

05:45.405 --> 05:46.938
Why are you still wearing that unitard?

05:46.973 --> 05:49.107
Can't get it off
'cause my hog's too big.

05:49.142 --> 05:50.675
Well, here, let me help you get it off.

05:50.711 --> 05:53.912
No, no, no, no, no, no.
I pooped. I pooped.

06:10.216 --> 06:11.449
What's going on with Nikkei?

06:16.956 --> 06:18.322
- What are you up to?
- Are you kidding?

06:18.358 --> 06:19.624
I've been looking at stocks all morning.

06:19.659 --> 06:21.359
I'm already up five percent on the day.

06:21.394 --> 06:23.961
Wow, good for you.
You're really taking to this.

06:23.997 --> 06:25.830
I wish I'd brought you in
on this earlier.

06:25.865 --> 06:27.965
Together, we're going to make a fortune.

06:28.001 --> 06:29.700
Well, now, hold on, Stewie.
I'm not some run-of-the-mill

06:29.736 --> 06:32.170
Wall Street scumbag only
in this for the profits.

06:32.205 --> 06:34.672
For every dollar I make, one goes to me,

06:34.707 --> 06:36.407
and one goes to charity.

06:36.442 --> 06:38.342
I'm gonna rent a Ferrari
and cruise the pier.

06:38.378 --> 06:39.811
You want in?

06:39.846 --> 06:42.680
Well, cancer's not going anywhere.

06:42.715 --> 06:44.782
I'm sorry, Billy,
you're one dollar short

06:44.818 --> 06:46.884
of being able to afford
the surgery you need.

06:46.920 --> 06:48.853
- Yeah!
- Money!

06:48.888 --> 06:51.189
Sweet. I know those guys.

06:57.096 --> 07:00.031
Wow, look at us, running the Clam.

07:00.066 --> 07:02.733
Joe, why are you dressed like that?

07:02.769 --> 07:04.068
'Cause I'm a mixologist.

07:04.103 --> 07:06.037
Oh, cool. What can you make?

07:06.072 --> 07:07.672
You name it, I can make it.

07:07.707 --> 07:09.240
Could I get an old-fashioned?

07:09.275 --> 07:11.843
Classic. Rum and Coke, coming right up.

07:11.878 --> 07:13.444
And could I get a Moscow mule?

07:13.479 --> 07:16.414
Rum and Coke for my comrade.

07:16.449 --> 07:19.183
- I'll have a whiskey...
- Rum...

07:19.219 --> 07:21.452
- sour.
- Coke. Coming right up.

07:21.487 --> 07:24.822
- Could I get a rum and Coke?
- Uh, Pepsi okay?

07:29.262 --> 07:30.962
Brian, I've got great news.

07:30.997 --> 07:32.330
We're going for a ride in the car?!

07:32.365 --> 07:34.699
No, our portfolio's up 30%.

07:34.734 --> 07:37.435
In fact, we're so successful
now, we have to make

07:37.470 --> 07:39.737
one of those sappy
investment commercials.

07:39.772 --> 07:43.140
<i>Thanks to my investments,
I've watched my money grow.</i>

07:43.176 --> 07:44.909
<i>And my little girl.</i>

07:44.944 --> 07:46.344
Dad?

07:46.379 --> 07:49.113
Thanks for making my big day possible.

07:49.148 --> 07:51.883
Don't thank me. Thank Fidelity.

07:51.918 --> 07:53.517
Okay, I'm ready to marry you now.

07:53.553 --> 07:55.353
Wait, what? No, I'm your dad.

07:55.388 --> 07:57.521
Yes, you are. This is what's happening.

07:57.557 --> 07:59.156
<i>Fidelity: We're there for you</i>

07:59.192 --> 08:01.592
<i>when your baby marries his dog-dad.</i>

08:04.631 --> 08:06.664
Stewie, why'd you bring me
all the way out here?

08:06.699 --> 08:08.466
Now that we're eccentric rich guys,

08:08.501 --> 08:11.702
we're going to go down 20,000
feet and pants James Cameron

08:11.738 --> 08:13.771
<i>while he's excavating the Titanic.</i>

08:18.511 --> 08:19.810
There he is.

08:19.846 --> 08:21.279
This is gonna be so great.

08:52.445 --> 08:54.312
Wow, business has really picked up.

08:54.347 --> 08:57.949
I think it's because of the
trivia night Quagmire started.

08:57.984 --> 08:59.216
Here we go, next question.

08:59.252 --> 09:00.785
And remember, no phones, people.

09:00.820 --> 09:02.687
Playing an honest game, no phones.

09:02.722 --> 09:04.121
Okay, "In what country..."

09:04.157 --> 09:06.157
No phones, I'm seeing phones.

09:06.192 --> 09:08.059
"In what country..." No phones.

09:08.094 --> 09:09.961
I've been pretty cool about this so far,

09:09.996 --> 09:11.329
it's a gentlemen's game.

09:11.364 --> 09:13.898
"In what country can you find
the monuments called..."

09:13.933 --> 09:15.399
I see phones. I see... all right,

09:15.435 --> 09:16.867
you know what, that's it,
trivia night over!

09:16.903 --> 09:18.836
Three cotton-picking weeks,

09:18.871 --> 09:20.471
and no one's gotten
a single answer wrong.

09:20.506 --> 09:21.672
Everyone's like, "Hey, settle down",

09:21.708 --> 09:22.807
we're not using our phones."

09:22.842 --> 09:25.042
I see you using your damn phones!

09:25.078 --> 09:27.044
Just... just give me my shift drink!

09:27.080 --> 09:28.980
Technically, you got to finish the game

09:29.015 --> 09:31.549
before you get your drink.

09:38.992 --> 09:40.992
"In which country..."

09:41.027 --> 09:43.094
And you know,
I think some people may be here

09:43.129 --> 09:44.595
because of me.

09:44.630 --> 09:47.431
I spread the word about
my sweet playlist.

09:47.467 --> 09:50.901
This is just a bunch of covers
of "Life Is A Highway."

09:50.937 --> 09:52.603
Yeah.

09:52.638 --> 09:54.038
Joe...

09:54.073 --> 09:56.173
you did a really great job.

09:56.209 --> 09:57.375
Thanks.

09:59.012 --> 10:00.878
♪ Life is a highway ♪

10:00.913 --> 10:02.480
♪ I want to... ♪

10:02.515 --> 10:04.882
(BLEEP), we went to the wrong place.

10:04.917 --> 10:06.684
Hey, guys, I had a great idea.

10:06.719 --> 10:08.586
You know how people love
mechanical bulls?

10:08.621 --> 10:11.655
Well, I got something even better!

10:13.326 --> 10:14.458
A real bull?

10:14.494 --> 10:16.627
If that thing gets mad,
it'll destroy the bar!

10:16.662 --> 10:18.062
Yeah, right. How can it get mad

10:18.097 --> 10:20.598
when I cinched its balls with my belt?

10:20.633 --> 10:23.401
See, it loves it here.
It's even picking out a song.

10:23.436 --> 10:26.704
♪ Life is a highway... ♪

10:26.739 --> 10:29.940
Excellent choice. You know,
not to tell tales out of school,

10:29.976 --> 10:33.277
but I sucked my first jug to this song.

10:33.312 --> 10:35.513
♪ If you are going my way ♪

10:35.548 --> 10:38.049
♪ I want to drive it ♪

10:38.084 --> 10:39.617
♪ All night long ♪

10:41.687 --> 10:44.989
♪ Life is a highway ♪

10:45.024 --> 10:47.324
♪ I want to ride it ♪

10:47.360 --> 10:49.527
♪ All night long ♪

10:49.562 --> 10:52.063
♪ Gimme, gimme, gimme, yeah ♪

10:52.098 --> 10:54.799
♪ If you are going my way ♪

10:54.834 --> 10:56.600
♪ I want to drive it ♪

10:56.636 --> 11:00.604
♪ All night long... ♪

11:02.141 --> 11:04.108
Edgar, do you know anything about this?

11:04.143 --> 11:05.509
What? N-No.

11:05.545 --> 11:06.644
Edgar?

11:06.679 --> 11:09.980
I was at Stanley Kaplan
preparing for the A.C.T.

11:10.016 --> 11:11.882
Well, then I am sanguine.

11:11.918 --> 11:13.050
Huh?

11:13.086 --> 11:14.819
Aha!

11:20.193 --> 11:21.826
Guys, wake up.

11:21.861 --> 11:23.661
Oh, man, the bull kicked our asses.

11:23.696 --> 11:25.096
And totally trashed the bar.

11:26.232 --> 11:27.731
What the hell is that?

11:27.767 --> 11:29.233
Oh, that's my ringtone.

11:29.268 --> 11:31.368
<i>It's from Game of Thrones
when Stannis's daughter</i>

11:31.404 --> 11:32.937
is burned alive at the stake.

11:32.972 --> 11:35.372
No way. It's from when Arya
and that other tiny girl

11:35.408 --> 11:36.640
fight to the death.

11:36.676 --> 11:38.642
Nah, that scream
is from the Red Wedding.

11:38.678 --> 11:42.379
It's the sound of a mama being
stabbed right in the baby.

11:42.415 --> 11:43.848
Hey, Jerome.

11:43.883 --> 11:45.049
Hey, Peter.

11:45.084 --> 11:46.717
I have some bad news.

11:46.752 --> 11:48.219
My mama...

11:49.655 --> 11:50.855
she's dead.

11:50.890 --> 11:52.156
Aw, man, that sucks, Lois.

11:52.191 --> 11:53.824
Your friend is probably just jealous.

11:53.860 --> 11:55.126
Peter.

11:55.161 --> 11:56.494
There's nothing left for me here,

11:56.529 --> 11:58.329
so I'm coming home tomorrow.

11:58.364 --> 12:01.866
That painting's all I got
to remember her by.

12:01.901 --> 12:04.001
You take good care of it, Peter.

12:04.036 --> 12:06.203
It's my prized possession.

12:10.443 --> 12:12.576
I'll see you tomorrow.

12:13.613 --> 12:15.079
What are we gonna do?

12:15.114 --> 12:17.515
Yeah. When Jerome sees that
painting, he's gonna kill us.

12:17.550 --> 12:19.650
Don't worry, guys,
he's got another one over there.

12:19.685 --> 12:21.318
Peter, that's Bruno Mars.

12:21.354 --> 12:22.419
Bruno Mars?

12:22.455 --> 12:23.487
Who's she?

12:23.523 --> 12:24.555
He's a man.

12:24.590 --> 12:25.823
And he's not even black.

12:25.858 --> 12:29.760
He's a beautiful,
mixed-up tomorrow person.

12:36.235 --> 12:37.501
What is this place?

12:37.537 --> 12:39.170
This is what you dragged me
out of the house

12:39.205 --> 12:40.538
first thing in the morning for?

12:40.573 --> 12:42.540
Yeah, it's a great company
I found to invest in.

12:42.575 --> 12:44.275
Korean. They make protein shakes.

12:44.310 --> 12:45.943
The profits are off the charts.

12:45.978 --> 12:47.578
Well, why is it
in the middle of nowhere?

12:47.613 --> 12:49.280
And why are there no windows?

12:49.315 --> 12:51.115
And why is there
a security guard out front?

12:51.150 --> 12:52.616
All these questions?

12:52.652 --> 12:55.186
This is why I didn't want to
let you have a soda in the car.

12:55.221 --> 12:56.453
It's not 'cause of the soda.

12:56.489 --> 12:58.389
God.

13:04.430 --> 13:05.563
Something's going on here.

13:05.598 --> 13:07.464
I'm taking a look.

13:07.500 --> 13:09.633
What are you doing?
It's just a protein shake.

13:09.669 --> 13:11.569
And it's the cheapest on the market.

13:15.274 --> 13:18.776
Uh, Brian, I think I know
why it's so cheap.

13:18.811 --> 13:22.179
They're made of dog meat.

13:22.215 --> 13:25.282
Oh, my God, look at
all those poor, sad dogs.

13:25.283 --> 13:28.482
♪ Life is a highway ♪

13:28.988 --> 13:34.425
♪ I want to ride it all night long ♪

13:34.460 --> 13:38.629
♪ Gimme, gimme, gimme, yeah. ♪

13:38.664 --> 13:41.365
They're all in trouble.
Even Rover Dangerfield.

13:41.400 --> 13:43.500
Oh, I tell you, I got to pay
more attention, you know?

13:43.536 --> 13:45.236
When the Korean guy said "shake,"

13:45.271 --> 13:46.470
I thought he meant my paw.

13:46.505 --> 13:48.272
Then he said I was gonna be protein.

13:48.307 --> 13:50.241
I said, "Damn right, I'm very pro-teen",

13:50.276 --> 13:51.642
I'm dating a 16-year-old."

13:51.677 --> 13:54.111
Oh, boy, I tell you,
I came in this place a purebred.

13:54.146 --> 13:55.579
Now I'm leaving it a pur├йe.

13:56.782 --> 13:58.983
No respect, no respect at all.

13:59.018 --> 14:00.384
Brian, let's get out of here.

14:00.419 --> 14:01.619
What do you mean? I'm taking a meeting.

14:01.654 --> 14:02.920
This company's worth a fortune.

14:02.955 --> 14:05.089
What? You still want to invest in this?

14:05.124 --> 14:07.057
- You can't be serious.
- Sorry, Stewie.

14:07.093 --> 14:10.194
Wall Street is a people-eat-dog
world, everyone knows that.

14:10.229 --> 14:11.328
Oh, my God.

14:11.364 --> 14:12.963
Brian, you've turned into a monster.

14:12.999 --> 14:14.164
Hey!

14:14.200 --> 14:16.400
That's offensive
to the monster community.

14:16.435 --> 14:17.901
Yeah, some of us are nice.

14:17.937 --> 14:19.236
Yeah, real nice.

14:19.272 --> 14:21.972
Weren't you charged with
sexually abusing a 16-year-old?

14:22.008 --> 14:23.707
Elmo's accuser recanted

14:23.743 --> 14:26.310
and admitted the relationship
was consensual.

14:26.345 --> 14:28.312
Yeah, but wasn't there another
case that was only thrown out

14:28.347 --> 14:30.514
because the statute
of limitations had expired?

14:30.549 --> 14:32.549
Elmo no comment.

14:34.787 --> 14:35.819
Cookie!

14:35.855 --> 14:37.187
He wants a cookie.

14:37.223 --> 14:38.622
Oh, I love the Muppets.

14:45.105 --> 14:47.538
I can't believe you still want
to invest in this.

14:47.573 --> 14:48.873
They use dog meat.

14:48.908 --> 14:51.375
How can you condone
the eating of other dogs?

14:51.411 --> 14:53.044
Oh, come on, Stewie, it's their way.

14:53.079 --> 14:54.979
Who are we to judge other cultures?

14:55.014 --> 14:56.914
Look, I'm investing in this company.

14:56.950 --> 14:58.683
And if you're too scared
to do it with me,

14:58.718 --> 15:00.318
then maybe I'm working
with the wrong partner.

15:00.353 --> 15:01.519
What are you talking about?

15:01.554 --> 15:03.120
I'm the one who taught you
how to invest.

15:03.156 --> 15:04.255
You can't ditch me.

15:04.290 --> 15:05.323
Sorry, Stewie.

15:05.358 --> 15:07.291
When I left you, I was but a learner.

15:07.327 --> 15:09.860
Now I am the master.

15:09.896 --> 15:11.095
Hee-ya!

15:11.130 --> 15:13.464
<i>Yeah. No one in Star Wars says "hee-ya."</i>

15:13.499 --> 15:14.799
You know what, Brian, forget it.

15:14.834 --> 15:16.667
We are done. You ruined this.

15:16.703 --> 15:19.570
We were a good team,
like Ricki and the Flash.

15:19.605 --> 15:21.138
I love you, Ricki.

15:21.174 --> 15:23.507
I love you, the Flash.

15:23.543 --> 15:25.142
Stewie, I don't think that's right.

15:25.178 --> 15:26.577
Ah, I didn't see the movie.

15:26.612 --> 15:28.245
Yeah, no, I didn't see it
either, but, yeah, the,

15:28.281 --> 15:30.414
"the Flash" was the name
of her rock band.

15:30.450 --> 15:31.682
Oh, you saw it.

15:31.718 --> 15:33.117
Yeah, I saw it.

15:33.152 --> 15:35.152
So did I.

15:38.324 --> 15:40.658
- This is stupid.
-Come on, guys. We got no choice.

15:40.693 --> 15:43.194
We have to paint that portrait
of Jerome's mother ourselves,

15:43.229 --> 15:45.029
and this is the only class in town.

15:45.064 --> 15:46.697
But aren't these classes
just for lame chicks

15:46.733 --> 15:49.433
who want an excuse to drink together?

15:52.372 --> 15:53.504
I'm having so much fun.

15:53.539 --> 15:54.605
Me, too.

15:54.640 --> 15:56.374
This wine is an artist.

15:56.409 --> 15:58.642
And it painted my smile.

16:01.347 --> 16:04.181
I don't think Paul
really wants to marry me.

16:04.217 --> 16:06.183
I, uh...

16:06.219 --> 16:08.686
I'm not sure what we're doing now.

16:14.727 --> 16:16.127
Hi, Brian Griffin.

16:16.162 --> 16:19.330
I have an appointment to see
your CEO about an investment.

16:19.365 --> 16:21.732
Ah, yes, we're waiting for you.

16:21.768 --> 16:25.236
Here, breathe deeply
into this investors' rag.

16:25.271 --> 16:28.005
All right. Now, I'm not sure
if I'm saying this right,

16:28.041 --> 16:31.242
but, uh, "Boo. Cocky."

16:37.050 --> 16:38.382
Can you believe Brian?

16:38.418 --> 16:40.918
Thinking he can fire me
when I'm the one who taught him?

16:40.953 --> 16:42.086
I have had it with him.

16:42.121 --> 16:43.320
Absolutely had it.

16:43.356 --> 16:44.688
He's just so selfish.

16:44.724 --> 16:45.990
He drives me crazy.

16:46.025 --> 16:48.292
I don't know why I put up
with it, I guess...

16:48.327 --> 16:51.295
I guess I just have
a forgiving personality.

16:51.330 --> 16:54.198
But enough about that, I'm
probably starting to bore you.

16:54.233 --> 16:57.101
It's just that whenever
I start talking about Brian,

16:57.136 --> 16:58.636
I lose all track of time.

16:58.671 --> 17:00.438
You would think,
after all these years together,

17:00.473 --> 17:03.407
that I could simply tell myself
enough is enough.

17:05.445 --> 17:07.378
You've reached
Stewie Griffin. Leave a message.

17:07.413 --> 17:09.447
Hey! Give me that phone.

17:09.482 --> 17:11.549
Stewie, it's Brian, you got
to help me, I'm gonna get ea...

17:11.584 --> 17:13.584
Damn it.

17:13.619 --> 17:16.687
Well, I guess Stewie's my only hope now.

17:16.722 --> 17:18.622
I can't believe I might die like this.

17:18.658 --> 17:21.392
I always thought I'd go
the way all dogs dream about:

17:21.427 --> 17:24.595
slowly, and at great
inconvenience to my owners.

17:24.630 --> 17:26.163
Come on, boy. Here we go.

17:26.199 --> 17:28.666
Here we go. Let's get you
to the living room.

17:29.969 --> 17:31.969
Lois, wrap one of his
"walking to the car" pills

17:32.004 --> 17:33.637
in roast beef and peanut butter.

17:33.673 --> 17:35.639
I'm gonna hold his hips
while he stands confused

17:35.675 --> 17:37.274
in front of the water dish.

17:37.310 --> 17:38.876
Go on, boy. It's right there.

17:44.117 --> 17:45.816
Come on, boy, it's right there.

17:45.852 --> 17:47.351
It's water. You like it.

17:50.123 --> 17:51.255
There you go.

17:51.290 --> 17:53.090
You're doing it yourself.

17:56.696 --> 17:58.496
Oh, God. Jerome's gonna be here
any minute,

17:58.531 --> 17:59.830
and then we're totally screwed.

17:59.866 --> 18:02.099
Well, I guess all we can do now
is the honorable thing:

18:02.135 --> 18:05.102
make realistic puppets
of ourselves to leave in the bar

18:05.138 --> 18:07.304
for Jerome to beat the crap out of.

18:09.442 --> 18:11.275
What the hell happened to my bar?

18:11.310 --> 18:12.776
And my painting!

18:12.812 --> 18:14.645
Well, don't just sit there staring at me

18:14.680 --> 18:17.715
with your limp limbs and
your straw-filled aid shirts.

18:20.453 --> 18:21.886
Wow, it's working!

18:21.921 --> 18:23.220
Good plan, Peter.

18:23.256 --> 18:24.688
Thanks, guys.

18:24.724 --> 18:26.924
Oh, no, I left the real me in there.

18:26.959 --> 18:29.026
He's falling for it, guys.

18:29.061 --> 18:30.694
He thinks I'm me.

18:35.568 --> 18:37.501
Come on, Stewie,
check your damn messages.

18:40.673 --> 18:42.640
God, that must be
where they do the deed.

18:42.675 --> 18:45.442
I hope it's at least
peaceful and humane.

18:46.479 --> 18:48.212
Vick!

18:48.247 --> 18:49.346
Oh, boy.

18:50.082 --> 18:52.650
And Eli Manning!

18:52.685 --> 18:54.552
Aw, I didn't know that
about Eli Manning.

18:54.587 --> 18:56.987
Oh, yeah. I'm a real idiot psychopath.

19:02.695 --> 19:03.894
What was that?

19:06.532 --> 19:07.698
What the...?

19:09.535 --> 19:11.001
Good job, Rupert.

19:11.037 --> 19:13.037
Now let's hope we can find Brian
before it's too late.

19:13.072 --> 19:14.772
Hey, don't touch me, I'm rich!

19:14.807 --> 19:18.542
Ugh, he just makes it
so difficult to be on his side.

19:21.013 --> 19:24.181
Oh, come on, there's got to be
a way we can work this out.

19:24.217 --> 19:25.749
Rupert, music!

19:26.886 --> 19:28.852
♪ Life is a highway ♪

19:28.888 --> 19:32.690
♪ I want to ride it all night long... ♪

19:32.725 --> 19:34.291
Oh, no. He knows Gymkata.

19:34.327 --> 19:35.526
There is no defense.

19:35.561 --> 19:38.762
Everyone, run for safety
over by those uneven bars.

19:38.798 --> 19:40.297
♪ I want to drive it... ♪

19:40.333 --> 19:42.266
Bad idea, buddy.

19:45.538 --> 19:47.705
♪ Life is a highway ♪

19:47.740 --> 19:51.375
♪ I want to ride it all night long ♪

19:53.112 --> 19:54.878
♪ Gimme, gimme, gimme, yeah ♪

19:54.914 --> 19:56.780
♪ If you're going my way ♪

19:56.816 --> 19:58.048
♪ I want to drive it... ♪

19:58.084 --> 20:00.551
Stewie! Oh, my God, thank you.

20:01.921 --> 20:03.220
I'm so sorry, Stewie.

20:03.256 --> 20:05.322
I guess I just lost my head.

20:05.358 --> 20:06.991
Well, lesson learned, Brian.

20:07.026 --> 20:08.759
Money doesn't buy happiness.

20:08.794 --> 20:10.227
This does:

20:10.263 --> 20:12.596
♪ Life is a highway ♪

20:12.632 --> 20:16.200
♪ I want to ride it all night long ♪

20:16.235 --> 20:19.103
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah ♪

20:19.138 --> 20:22.106
♪ If you're going my way ♪

20:22.141 --> 20:26.410
♪ I want to drive it all night long ♪

20:26.445 --> 20:27.678
♪ Gimme, gimme, gimme, yeah. ♪

20:34.238 --> 20:37.372
Wow, Stewie. I am so sorry
I became such a jerk.

20:37.407 --> 20:39.674
But I guess I learned my lesson
about the evils of Wall Street.

20:39.710 --> 20:41.009
What are you talking about?

20:41.044 --> 20:42.510
This isn't about Wall Street,
this is about you.

20:42.546 --> 20:43.745
Me?

20:43.780 --> 20:45.180
I've been investing
in the market forever,

20:45.215 --> 20:46.348
and doing just fine.

20:46.383 --> 20:47.582
You did it for one week,

20:47.618 --> 20:49.851
and were literally eating your own kind.

20:49.886 --> 20:51.186
This isn't about Wall Street.

20:51.221 --> 20:52.687
I cannot stress that enough.

20:52.723 --> 20:54.689
Well, money is the root of all evil.

20:54.725 --> 20:56.191
No, it's not. It's just you.

20:56.226 --> 20:58.260
Hello, others, I am the father.

20:58.295 --> 20:59.427
Where is the mother,

20:59.463 --> 21:02.530
and what kind of sex
does she like to have?

21:02.531 --> 21:05.531
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru